<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/cleaning-of-hypo-box> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Cleaning of Hypo Box" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Hospitalised patients with diabetes mellitus" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "cleaning-of-hypo-box" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "A hard plastic hypo box can be cleaned with a damp cloth or clinell wipe, and should be cleaned in accordance with your Trust’s equipment cleaning procedures." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A hard plastic hypo box can be cleaned with a damp cloth or clinell wipe, and should be cleaned in accordance with your Trust’s equipment cleaning procedures." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/communicate-significant-diabetes-treatment-changes-or-monitoring-recommendations> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Communicate significant diabetes treatment changes or monitoring recommendations" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "communicate-significant-diabetes-treatment-changes-or-monitoring-recommendations" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "If the diabetes treatment has changed significantly on discharge, or enhanced monitoring has been recommended, please communicate this to their primary care team in a timely manner." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "l\t If the diabetes treatment has changed significantly on discharge, or enhanced \nmonitoring has been recommended, please communicate this to their primary \ncare team in a timely manner." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/communication-with-primary-care-after-significant-treatment-changes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Communication with Primary Care After Significant Treatment Changes" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes in hospital with significant treatment changes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "communication-with-primary-care-after-significant-treatment-changes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "Please consider how best to communicate with colleagues in primary care if there have been significant treatment changes. This would be particularly important if treatment changes were temporary and required review (e.g. withholding a sulfonylurea and metformin after hypoglycaemia during a period of acute kidney injury)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Please consider how best to communicate with colleagues in primary care if there have been significant treatment changes. This would be particularly important if treatment changes were temporary and required review (e.g. withholding a sulfonylurea and metformin after hypoglycaemia during a period of acute kidney injury)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/complete-incident-form-if-appropriate> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Complete incident form if appropriate" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "complete-incident-form-if-appropriate" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Consider completing an incident form (e.g. DATIX) if appropriate." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When hypoglycaemia has been successfully treated  \n(after following the initial steps outlined in algorithms A-E) \n\nl\t Consider completing an incident form (e.g. DATIX) if appropriate." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/concurrent-use-of-medicines-with-hypoglycaemic-agents> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent use of medicines with hypoglycaemic agents" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "concurrent-use-of-medicines-with-hypoglycaemic-agents" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Safety" ;
    dmo:statement "Concurrent use of medicines with hypoglycaemic agents e.g. warfarin, quinine, salicylates, fibrates, sulphonamides (including cotrimoxazole), linezolid, monoamine oxidase inhibitors, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), probenecid, somatostatin analogues, selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors. Do not stop or withhold medication, discuss with the medical team or pharmacist" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "l Concurrent use of medicines with hypoglycaemic agents e.g. warfarin, quinine, salicylates, fibrates, sulphonamides (including cotrimoxazole), linezolid, monoamine oxidase inhibitors, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), probenecid, somatostatin analogues, selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors. Do not stop or withhold medication, discuss with the medical team or pharmacist" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/consider-dose-adjustment-in-high-risk-individuals-with-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Consider dose adjustment in high-risk individuals with hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Older adults with T2DM on high-dose sulfonylurea therapy, especially with comorbidities such as UTI or AKI" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "consider-dose-adjustment-in-high-risk-individuals-with-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "An 84-year-old woman with T2DM on high dose sulfonylurea therapy admitted with a urinary tract infection and acute kidney injury would be at substantially higher risk of hypoglycaemia. Dose adjustment may well then be appropriate, possibly proactively but certainly if readings in the range of 4.0-6.0mmol/L were being recorded." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "An 84-year-old woman with T2DM on high dose sulfonylurea therapy admitted with a urinary tract infection and acute kidney injury would be at substantially higher risk of hypoglycaemia. Dose adjustment may well then be appropriate, possibly proactively but certainly if readings in the range of 4.0-6.0mmol/L were being recorded." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/consider-intravenous-infusion-of-10-glucose-at-100ml-hr-until-no-longer-nil-by-mouth-or-reviewed-by-medical-team> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Consider intravenous infusion of 10% glucose at 100ml/hr until no longer 'Nil by Mouth' or reviewed by medical team" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults with diabetes in hospital who have experienced hypoglycaemia and are 'Nil by Mouth'" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "consider-intravenous-infusion-of-10-glucose-at-100ml-hr-until-no-longer-nil-by-mouth-or-reviewed-by-medical-team" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Once blood glucose is greater than 4.0mmol/L and the person has recovered consider intravenous infusion of 10% glucose at a rate of 100ml/hr until they are no longer ‘Nil by Mouth’ or have been reviewed by the medical team." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Once blood glucose is greater than 4.0mmol/L and the person has recovered consider intravenous infusion of 10% glucose at a rate of 100ml/hr until they are no longer ‘Nil by Mouth’ or have been reviewed by the medical team." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/consider-medical-or-disn-review-if-cause-not-identifiable> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Consider medical or DISN review if cause not identifiable" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "consider-medical-or-disn-review-if-cause-not-identifiable" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "Unless the cause is easily identifiable and both the nursing staff and the person with diabetes is confident steps can be taken to avoid future events, a medical or Diabetes Inpatient Specialist Nurse (DISN) review should be considered.  If the hypoglycaemia event was severe or recurrent, or if the person voices concerns then a review is indicated" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When hypoglycaemia has been successfully treated  \n(after following the initial steps outlined in algorithms A-E) \n\nl\t Consider completing an incident form (e.g. DATIX) if appropriate. \nl\t If “hypo boxes” have been used then restock as appropriate. \nl\t Identify the risk factors for hypoglycaemia (see Table 2). \nl\t Take measures to avoid hypoglycaemia in the future.  The Inpatient Diabetes \nTeam can be contacted to discuss this. \nl\t Unless the cause is easily identifiable and both the nursing staff and the person \nwith diabetes is  confident steps can be taken to avoid future events, a medical \n or Diabetes Inpatient Specialist Nurse (DISN) review should be considered.  If the \nhypoglycaemia event was severe or recurrent, or if the person voices concerns \nthen a review is indicated" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/consider-reducing-insulin-or-sulfonylurea-dose-active-at-time-of-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Consider reducing insulin or sulfonylurea dose active at time of hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "consider-reducing-insulin-or-sulfonylurea-dose-active-at-time-of-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Medical team (or DISN if referred) to consider reducing the dose of insulin or sulfonylurea that would have been active at the time of the hypoglycaemic event.  This is to prevent further hypoglycaemia episodes occurring." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "l\t Medical team (or DISN if referred) to consider reducing the dose of insulin or \nsulfonylurea that would have been active at the time of the hypoglycaemic event.  \nThis is to prevent further hypoglycaemia episodes occurring." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/consideration-of-prolonged-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Consideration of Prolonged Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People who have experienced hypoglycaemia and are at risk of prolonged hypoglycaemia due to long-acting insulin or sulfonylurea therapy" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "consideration-of-prolonged-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Conditional" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "After acute treatment, consideration should be given to whether the hypoglycaemia is likely to be prolonged, i.e. as a result of long-acting insulin or sulfonylurea therapy; these people may require a continuous infusion of glucose to maintain blood glucose levels." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "After acute treatment, consideration should be given to whether the hypoglycaemia is likely to be prolonged, i.e. as a result of long-acting insulin or sulfonylurea therapy; these people may require a continuous infusion of glucose to maintain blood glucose levels." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/continue-blood-glucose-monitoring-for-24-to-48-hours-after-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Continue Blood Glucose Monitoring for 24 to 48 Hours After Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are unconscious and/or having seizures and/or are very aggressive" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "continue-blood-glucose-monitoring-for-24-to-48-hours-after-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours. Ask the person to continue this at home if they are to be discharged." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "14. Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours. Ask the person to continue this at home if they are to be discharged." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/continue-capillary-blood-glucose-monitoring-for-at-least-24-to-48-hours> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Continue capillary blood glucose monitoring for at least 24 to 48 hours" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults with diabetes in hospital who have experienced hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "continue-capillary-blood-glucose-monitoring-for-at-least-24-to-48-hours" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/continue-iv-insulin-after-hypoglycaemia-recovery-with-dose-review> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Continue IV Insulin After Hypoglycaemia Recovery with Dose Review" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are unconscious and/or having seizures and/or are very aggressive" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "continue-iv-insulin-after-hypoglycaemia-recovery-with-dose-review" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If the person was on IV insulin, continue to check blood glucose every 15 minutes until above 4.0mmol/L, then re-start IV insulin after review of dose regimen to try and prevent hypoglycaemia recurrence. Consider concurrent IV 10% glucose infusion at 100ml/hr and/or stepping down the insulin increments on the variable scale if appropriate (check local Trust guidance)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "12. If the person was on IV insulin, continue to check blood glucose every 15 minutes until above 4.0mmol/L, then re-start IV insulin after review of dose regimen to try and prevent hypoglycaemia recurrence. Consider concurrent IV 10% glucose infusion at 100ml/hr and/or stepping down the insulin increments on the variable scale if appropriate (check local Trust guidance)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/contraindication-of-im-and-subcutaneous-injection-for-glucose> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Contraindication of IM and subcutaneous injection for glucose" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "contraindication-of-im-and-subcutaneous-injection-for-glucose" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "IM injection: Contraindicated Subcutaneous injection: Contraindicated" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "IM injection: Contraindicated Subcutaneous injection: Contraindicated" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/daily-check-of-hypo-box> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Daily Check of Hypo Box" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Hospitalised patients with diabetes mellitus" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "daily-check-of-hypo-box" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "“Hypo box” contents should be checked on a daily basis to ensure it is complete and in date." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Appendix 1 “Hypo box” contents should be checked on a daily basis to ensure it is complete and in date. It is the responsibility of the member of staff who uses any contents to replenish them after use." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/discuss-subsequent-diabetes-treatment-if-unsure> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Discuss subsequent diabetes treatment if unsure" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "discuss-subsequent-diabetes-treatment-if-unsure" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If unsure of subsequent diabetes treatment, discuss with the inpatient diabetes team (e.g. it may be safe to omit a meal time bolus dose of rapid-acting insulin if the person has declined food and taken their usual basal insulin)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "l\t Please DO NOT omit the next insulin injection or start variable rate intravenous \ninsulin infusion to ‘stabilise’ blood glucose.  If unsure of subsequent diabetes \ntreatment, discuss with the inpatient diabetes team (e.g. it may be safe to omit a \nmeal time bolus dose of rapid-acting insulin if the person has declined food and \ntaken their usual basal insulin)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/do-not-omit-insulin-injection-if-due> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Do not omit insulin injection if due" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are conscious, orientated and able to swallow" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "do-not-omit-insulin-injection-if-due" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "DO NOT omit insulin injection if due.  The insulin injection about to be given is unlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode and so should not be omitted.  However, consideration will have to be given as to which insulin dose was active at the time of the hypoglycaemic episode and so a review of their insulin regimen is likely to be required." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "9. DO NOT omit insulin injection if due.  The insulin injection about to be given is unlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode and so should not be omitted.  However, consideration will have to be given as to which insulin dose was active at the time of the hypoglycaemic episode and so a review of their insulin regimen is likely to be required." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "7. DO NOT omit insulin injection if due. The insulin injection about to be given is \nunlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode \nand so should not be omitted." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/do-not-omit-insulin-injection-if-due-after-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
