    dmo:evidenceQuote "11. DO NOT omit insulin injection if due. The insulin injection about to be given is unlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode and so should not be omitted. However, consideration will have to be given as to which insulin dose was active at the time of the hypoglycaemic episode and so a review of their insulin regimen is likely to be required." ;
