<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/do-not-treat-isolated-hyperglycaemia-spikes-with-stat-doses-of-rapid-acting-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Do not treat isolated hyperglycaemia spikes with stat doses of rapid-acting insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "do-not-treat-isolated-hyperglycaemia-spikes-with-stat-doses-of-rapid-acting-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Safety" ;
    dmo:statement "Please DO NOT treat isolated spikes of hyperglycaemia with ‘stat’ doses of rapid-acting insulin. Instead maintain regular capillary blood glucose monitoring and adjust normal insulin or sulfonylurea doses only if a particular pattern emerges." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "l\t Please DO NOT treat isolated spikes of hyperglycaemia with ‘stat’ doses of rapid-\nacting insulin. Instead maintain regular capillary blood glucose monitoring and \nadjust normal insulin or sulfonylurea doses only if a particular pattern emerges." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/document-hypoglycaemia-event-and-continue-monitoring> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Document hypoglycaemia event and continue monitoring" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are conscious, orientated and able to swallow" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "document-hypoglycaemia-event-and-continue-monitoring" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours.  Ask the person to continue this at home if they are to be discharged.  Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local Diabetes Inpatient Team.  An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes website (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "11. Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours.  Ask the person to continue this at home if they are to be discharged.  Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local Diabetes Inpatient Team.  An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes website (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "9. Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose \nmonitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours.  Ask the person to continue this \nat home if they are to be discharged." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/document-hypoglycaemia-event-in-clinical-record> a dmo:Recommendation ;
