<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/hypo-box-contents> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Hypo Box Contents" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Hospitalised patients with diabetes mellitus" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "hypo-box-contents" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Example contents of a hypo box include a laminated copy of the hypoglycaemia algorithm, 2x 200ml cartons of pure fruit juice, 2x packets of dextrose tablets, 1x mini pack of biscuits, 3x tubes of 40% glucose gel, 20% glucose IV solution (100ml vial) with infusion set, 1x green cannula 18G, 1x grey cannula 16G, 1x 10ml sterile syringe, 3x 10ml sodium chloride 0.9% ampoules for flush, 1x green sterile needle 21G, chlorhexidine spray/alcohol wipes, 1x IV dressing, 10% glucose for IV infusion (500ml bag) with infusion set, audit form, instructions on where to send audit form and replenish supplies, and 1x Glucagon pack." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Example contents of a hypo box l Copy of hypoglycaemia algorithm (laminated and attached to inside of lid) l 2x 200ml carton of pure fruit juice l 2x packets of dextrose tablets l 1x mini pack of biscuits (source of long-acting carbohydrate) l 3 x tubes (1 box) 40% glucose gel l 20% glucose IV solution (100ml vial) with infusion set l 1x green cannula 18G l 1x grey cannula 16G l 1x 10ml sterile syringe l 3 x 10ml sodium chloride 0.9% ampoules for flush l 1x green sterile needle 21G l Chlorhexidine spray/alcohol wipes l 1x IV dressing (cannula cover) l 10% glucose for IV infusion (500ml bag) with infusion set l Audit form l Instructions on where to send audit form and replenish supplies l 1x Glucagon pack – to be kept in the nearest drug fridge or labelled with reduced expiry date of 18 months if stored at room temperature" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/hypo-boxes-should-be-available-in-clinical-areas> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Hypo boxes should be available in clinical areas" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "hypo-boxes-should-be-available-in-clinical-areas" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Hypo boxes should be available in clinical areas" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Easily accessible quick- and long-acting carbohydrate must be available in your clinical area (ideally located in a hypo box) and all staff should be aware of its location." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

