<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/increased-long-acting-carbohydrate-after-glucagon-use> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Increased Long-Acting Carbohydrate After Glucagon Use" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are conscious but confused, disorientated, unable to cooperate or aggressive but are able to swallow" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "increased-long-acting-carbohydrate-after-glucagon-use" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "People given glucagon require a larger portion of long-acting carbohydrate (40g) to replenish glycogen stores (double the suggested amounts below) although nausea associated with glucagon injections may be an issue." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People given glucagon require a larger portion of long-acting carbohydrate (40g) to replenish glycogen stores (double the suggested amounts below) although nausea associated with glucagon injections may be an issue." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/individualised-approach-to-hypoglycaemia-management> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Individualised approach to hypoglycaemia management" ;
    dmo:populationScope "All inpatients with diabetes, especially when managing hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "individualised-approach-to-hypoglycaemia-management" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "An individualised approach is often helpful and advice should be sought from the inpatient diabetes team if unsure." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "An individualised approach is often helpful and advice should be sought from the inpatient diabetes team if unsure." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/individualised-glycaemic-targets-for-insulin-pump-users-and-wearable-glucose-sensor-users> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Individualised Glycaemic Targets for Insulin Pump Users and Wearable Glucose Sensor Users" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes using insulin pumps and/or wearable glucose sensors" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "individualised-glycaemic-targets-for-insulin-pump-users-and-wearable-glucose-sensor-users" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "For some people, especially those using insulin pumps and/or wearable glucose sensors, a range of 4-6mmol/L may be their normal when they are not eating. It is important to have a discussion with them about the need to avoid severe hypoglycaemia, they may need to aim for higher glucose levels than they are used to." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For some people, especially those using insulin pumps and/or wearable glucose sensors, a range of 4-6mmol/L may be their normal when they are not eating. It is important to have a discussion with them about the need to avoid severe hypoglycaemia, they may need to aim for higher glucose levels than they are used to." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-injection-should-not-be-omitted> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Injection Should Not Be Omitted" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are conscious but confused, disorientated, unable to cooperate or aggressive but are able to swallow" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-injection-should-not-be-omitted" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "DO NOT omit insulin injection if due. The insulin injection about to be given is unlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode and so should not be omitted." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "DO NOT omit insulin injection if due. The insulin injection about to be given is unlikely to be the insulin dose that was active at the time of the hypoglycaemia episode and so should not be omitted." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/intervention-for-looming-hypoglycaemia-in-blood-glucose-range-4-0-6-0mmol-l> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Intervention for Looming Hypoglycaemia in Blood Glucose Range 4.0-6.0mmol/L" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes in hospital with blood glucose level of 4.0-6.0mmol/L" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "intervention-for-looming-hypoglycaemia-in-blood-glucose-range-4-0-6-0mmol-l" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "The risk of looming hypoglycaemia should be considered in people who have a blood glucose level of 4.0-6.0mmol/L while in hospital. For the majority of people on any insulin preparation and/or any insulin secretagogues, consider intervening at a capillary blood glucose (CBG) of <6.0mmol/L to prevent hypoglycaemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The risk of looming hypoglycaemia should be considered in people who have a blood glucose level of 4.0-6.0mmol/L while in hospital. For the majority of people on any insulin preparation and/or any insulin secretagogues, consider intervening at a capillary blood glucose (CBG) of <6.0mmol/L to prevent hypoglycaemia." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/intravenous-glucose> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Intravenous glucose" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "intravenous-glucose" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Intravenous glucose is the preferred option due to faster recovery of blood glucose levels and lower treatment failure rate compared to glucagon." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, it can only be used once with the slower recovery and higher treatment failure rate making intravenous glucose the preferred option (60)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/iv-glucose-or-glucagon-can-be-given-without-a-prescription-in-emergency> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "IV glucose or glucagon can be given without a prescription in emergency" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "iv-glucose-or-glucagon-can-be-given-without-a-prescription-in-emergency" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "IV glucose or glucagon can be given without a prescription to treat hypoglycaemia but that your local organisation might not permit this" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "It is important to emphasise that in the emergency situation IV glucose or glucagon can be given without a prescription to treat hypoglycaemia but that your local organisation might not permit this (69)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/joint-decision-on-intervention-threshold-for-blood-glucose> a dmo:Recommendation ;
