<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/proactive-intervention-for-looming-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Proactive intervention for looming hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes in hospital on glucose lowering medications such as insulin secretagogues or insulin therapy" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "proactive-intervention-for-looming-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "For people with diabetes in hospital, it may be appropriate to act proactively to prevent hypoglycaemia at higher blood glucose levels. A blood glucose value between 4.0 to 6.0mmol/L could indicate looming hypoglycaemia; particularly if repeated episodes showed a particular pattern of glucose measurements below 6.0mmol/L were occurring. This may require oral or intravenous carbohydrate depending on the clinical situation." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "While the treatment threshold for hypoglycaemia remains at less than 4.0mmol/L, for people with diabetes in hospital, it may be appropriate to act proactively to prevent hypoglycaemia at higher blood glucose levels. This would be especially relevant for those on glucose lowering medications such as insulin secretagogues (e.g. sulfonylureas) or insulin therapy. A blood glucose value between 4.0 to 6.0mmol/L could indicate looming hypoglycaemia; particularly if repeated episodes showed a particular pattern of glucose measurements below 6.0mmol/L were occurring. This may require oral or intravenous carbohydrate depending on the clinical situation; if the person is fasting for" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/promotion-of-hypoglycaemia-rescue-treatment-prescription> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Promotion of Hypoglycaemia Rescue Treatment Prescription" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes in hospital on insulin or sulfonylurea therapy" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "promotion-of-hypoglycaemia-rescue-treatment-prescription" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Promote the prescription of hypoglycaemia “rescue” treatment for all people with diabetes in hospital on insulin or sulfonylurea therapy. This could involve a “PRN (pro re nata)” or “as needed” prescription of intravenous (IV) glucose and/or intramuscular (IM) glucagon." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Promote the prescription of hypoglycaemia “rescue” treatment for all people with diabetes in hospital on insulin or sulfonylurea therapy. This could involve a “PRN (pro re nata)” or “as needed” prescription of intravenous (IV) glucose and/or intramuscular (IM) glucagon." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/provide-hypoglycaemia-education-or-refer-to-diabetes-inpatient-team> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Provide hypoglycaemia education or refer to Diabetes Inpatient Team" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "provide-hypoglycaemia-education-or-refer-to-diabetes-inpatient-team" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local Diabetes Inpatient Team.  An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes website (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "9. Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose \nmonitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours.  Ask the person to continue this \nat home if they are to be discharged.  Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local \nDiabetes Inpatient Team.  An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes \nwebsite (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/provide-hypoglycaemia-education-or-refer-to-local-diabetes-inpatient-team> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Provide Hypoglycaemia Education or Refer to Local Diabetes Inpatient Team" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults who are unconscious and/or having seizures and/or are very aggressive" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "provide-hypoglycaemia-education-or-refer-to-local-diabetes-inpatient-team" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local Diabetes Inpatient Team. An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes website (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "14. Document event in the individual’s clinical record. Ensure regular capillary blood glucose monitoring is continued for at least 24 to 48 hours. Ask the person to continue this at home if they are to be discharged. Give hypoglycaemia education or refer to local Diabetes Inpatient Team. An education leaflet is available from the Trend Diabetes website (https://trenddiabetes.online/) (log in required)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/rapid-acting-carbohydrate-for-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Rapid-Acting Carbohydrate for Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes experiencing hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "rapid-acting-carbohydrate-for-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "People with diabetes experiencing hypoglycaemia require a rapid-acting carbohydrate to restore euglycaemia (usually 4.0-7.0mmol/L). The rapid-acting carbohydrate should be followed up by giving long-acting carbohydrate either as a snack or as part of a planned meal." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People with diabetes experiencing hypoglycaemia require a rapid-acting carbohydrate to restore euglycaemia (usually 4.0-7.0mmol/L). The rapid-acting carbohydrate should be followed up by giving long-acting carbohydrate either as a snack or as part of a planned meal." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/rate-of-administration-for-20-glucose-infusion> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Rate of administration for 20% glucose infusion" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "rate-of-administration-for-20-glucose-infusion" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Give 100ml of 20% glucose over 10-15 minutes (set rate 300-400mL/hour), or 200ml 10% glucose over 10-15 minutes (set rate 600-800mL/hour). Use an infusion pump if available. For the initial emergency management of hypoglycaemia this may be administered via a giving set alone." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Give 100ml of 20% glucose * over 10-15 minutes (set rate 300-400mL/hour), or 200ml 10% glucose over 10-15 minutes (set rate 600-800mL/hour). Use an infusion pump if available. For the initial emergency management of hypoglycaemia this may be administered via a giving set alone." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/re-start-feed-after-hypoglycaemia-treatment> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Re-start feed after hypoglycaemia treatment" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "re-start-feed-after-hypoglycaemia-treatment" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Restart feed" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "6. Once blood glucose is above 4.0mmol/L and the person has recovered:\n• Restart feed" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_01_hypo_guideline_with_qr_code_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/re-start-feed-to-rapidly-deliver-15-20g-carbohydrate> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Re-start feed to rapidly deliver 15–20g carbohydrate" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults with diabetes in hospital receiving enteral feeding and experiencing hypoglycaemia" ;
